@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ Version 1.8.0 (2026-10-06)
 
 Enhancements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
+- Update :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024` to version 2 of the release (Zenodo 17940098): six more subjects (9-14) from a second study, unilateral movements only; the EEG files of subjects 1-8 are unchanged. Add a ``rest`` class placed 3 s before each correct movement onset whose preceding rest lasted at least 5 s, so all 14 subjects can be evaluated with ``unilateral`` versus ``rest``. The second study has no motion-tracking marker, so its movement onset is the release of the right hand switch, which follows the motion-tracking onset by a median of 54 ms in the first study. Mark the dataset as movement execution (``detected_paradigm="motor_execution"``) and describe the trial protocol as the authors do: a rest of at least 5 s, the movement onset at 0 s, then self-paced execution (:gh:`1333` reported by `Niklas Kueper`_, fixed by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Add the tutorial :ref:`sphx_glr_auto_examples_how_to_benchmark_plot_cross_system_transfer_maskedmean.py`: cross-system transfer with a minimum distance to masked Riemannian mean, on datasets recorded with different montages and sampling rates, pooled in a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset` and evaluated with :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossSubjectEvaluation` (``cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut, groups="device"``). To support it, the evaluations route any metadata column of the training trials (``device``, ``dataset``, ``subject``...) to the pipeline steps that request it with scikit-learn metadata routing (``set_fit_request(device=True)``), and :class:`~moabb.datasets.fake.FakeDataset` takes a ``device`` (:gh:`1305` by `Quentin Barthelemy`_).
 - The metadata returned by :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data` has two new columns: ``dataset``, the code of the dataset each trial comes from (for a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset`, the dataset the subject comes from), and ``device``, the recording device. ``device`` is the canonical name of ``METADATA.acquisition.hardware`` given by :func:`moabb.datasets.metadata.devices.canonical_device` (the 107 free-text descriptions map to 30 devices, e.g. every spelling of the g.tec g.USBamp; ``"unknown"`` when the dataset gives none); :class:`moabb.datasets.Peters2026` returns the DSI-24 or DSI-Flex of each visit. ``CrossSubjectEvaluation(cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut, groups="dataset")`` holds out one dataset at a time and ``groups="device"`` one device at a time, and :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossDatasetSplitter` works on paradigm output (:gh:`1328` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data` no longer fails when the recordings it stacks have different channels or numbers of samples, e.g. datasets with different montages or sampling rates pooled in a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset`: it returns a nested object array of shape ``(n_trials,)`` holding each trial's ``(n_channels, n_times)`` array, and the evaluations accept it, so leave-one-dataset-out runs with :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossSubjectEvaluation` and ``cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut``. Recordings of one shape still give a regular array; ``return_epochs=True`` raises a clear error for such recordings, as ``mne.Epochs`` cannot hold them (:gh:`1327` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
@@ -96,6 +97,7 @@ Requirements
 
 Bugs
 ~~~~
+- Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024` keeping error trials (rest shorter than 5 s, marker ``S3``) and additional trials (``S27``) as movement events: only onsets followed by the end-of-correct-trial marker ``S128`` are kept, 40 per recording set. Also download the subjects a partial cache lacks instead of returning no runs: ``data_path`` checked only that the dataset folder existed, so a cache from version 1 or from the NEMAR deposit (subjects 1-8) would have loaded subjects 9-14 empty (:gh:`1333` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Cho2017` giving the pre-cue segment a class-dependent offset. The GigaDB files store each class as a stream of tiled 7-s trial blocks (2 s fixation, then the cue), and the loader removed the mean of each class stream as a whole; since some participants make a sustained eye movement toward the imagined hand after the cue, that mean differs by class, so without a high-pass filter (``fmin=None``) the pre-cue segment of every trial carried an offset of about half the post-cue step, with the opposite sign. The loader now removes from each block the mean of its own fixation period (subject 5, F8-F7 in the second before the cue, right minus left: -4313 before, +7 after, in file units). The default 8-32 Hz band and the default 0-3 s interval give identical data. A high-pass of 0.1-1 Hz removes the mean of the tiled block pattern itself and puts the offset back whatever the loader does; the docstring now documents the data layout and recommends the default ``fmin`` or a pre-cue ``baseline`` in that case. Adds an offline regression test on a synthetic tiled file (:gh:`1340` by `Yiheng Li`_).
 - Fix :func:`moabb.analysis.plotting.summary_plot` raising ``ValueError: The truth value of a Series is ambiguous`` when two pipeline names shorten to the same first word, such as ``Tangent Space LR`` and ``Tangent Space SVM Grid`` from ``pipelines/``. It now keeps the full names and logs a warning, the same as ``analyze`` already does (by `Iain`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Gao2026` returning EEG amplitudes 256 times too small. The loader divided every EEG channel by 256, assuming the BDF header's 16-bit digital range (-32768..32767) was wrong for 24-bit data. It is not: each released file stores values within that range and sets its physical range to its own largest sample (10 mV to 375 mV across the 125 recordings), so MNE's header calibration already gives the correct amplitudes (median channel SD about 9 µV at 1-40 Hz, Fp1/Fp2 blinks about 250 µV, occipital visual evoked responses about 10 µV; 0.03 µV, 1 µV and 0.04 µV after the division). Adds a regression test on a synthetic BDF stored the same way (:gh:`1330` by `Adam Rolander`_).
